  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Initial Requirements**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the initial requirements for \"Repert\303\263rio Autom\303\241tico,\" specifically establishing the application\'s name and description as a mobile-first PWA. I\'m aiming for a straightforward, user-friendly name, and a clear, concise description that will provide users with essential information about the app\'s functionality. My priority is to create an intuitive experience.\n\n\n**Refining PWA Specifications**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the core domain and entities for the application. Specifically, I am focusing on the \"Cat\303\241logo,\" \"Setlist,\" \"Bloco,\" and the \"M\303\272sica do Bloco\" entities, outlining their key fields and relationships. My recent update involved including a server-side Gemini API capability and updating `metadata.json`. I\'m establishing the structure for data management, aiming for user-friendliness in handling song libraries, setlists, and performance blocks. I am also working to ensure each element is clearly defined.\n\n\n**Developing Cifra Features**\n\nI\'m currently working on Cifra features, specifically the auto-construction of Cifra Club URLs. This involves calculating the `?tom={N}` parameter, handling key differences, and normalizing keys like \"D\303\263\" to \"C\". I\'m also planning for manual adjustments to URLs and implementing an in-app Webview for Cifra viewing, with a browser fallback.\n\n\n**Implementing Backend and PWA**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the backend and PWA aspects. I\'ve decided to provide a complete local/in-memory backend with indexedDB/localStorage mock capabilities, or a Supabase client mock with real-time sync. This supports both real Supabase environment variables and effortless local storage mode. I\'m ensuring the client state engine (Zustand + React Query) works flawlessly in the browser preview with mock auth and offline PWA caching. I\'m also including `manifest.json` and `sw.js` for offline caching and PWA installation.\n\n\n**Designing UI Navigation**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in designing the user interface and navigation flow. I\'m focusing on a clean, PT-BR language UI with dark/light mode support, and a streamlined bottom navigation bar featuring just three icons: Setlists, Cat\303\241logo, and Perfil. The Home/Setlists View includes setlist listings, an onboarding state with a clear call-to-action, and a modal for setlist creation and management. The Setlist Detail View will have a top bar for core actions and an organized list of draggable blocks, complete with search and filter capabilities, and I\'m planning for a focused block view upon tapping a block. The plan is to include member management for invitations and permissions.\n\n\n**Enhancing Block View**\n\nI\'m now refining the Block View to increase usability. I\'ve implemented an immersive mode where the bottom bar disappears for a cleaner experience, and included a discrete \"Voltar\" button at the top to return to the setlist. Each block item now has the block title, a theme badge, and a vertical numbered list. The layout for each song in the block is formatted as \"01. Wonderwall \342\200\224 C \342\206\222 D,\" with the original key subtly displayed on the left of the arrow, and the requested key bolded on the right. Tapping the requested key now opens an inline edit text field. There\'s a dedicated Cifra icon for each song that opens a webview or modal iframe overlay. Users can reorder songs within a block using up/down buttons or a drag handle. A new add song button opens a bottom sheet search modal across the catalog, with options to select and add, or create a new song if it doesn\'t exist.\n\n**Adding Catalog Functionality**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the Cat\303\241logo View. This view is now an alphabetical list by song name with the artist and original key for each song listed. I\'ve added a search bar that can look up songs by name or artist. I\'ve also implemented a modal for adding new catalog songs, with fields for name, artist (mandatory), and original key. I\'m working on the ability to edit and delete catalog songs, and I\'ll include a double confirmation modal that will show the user how many blocks are affected.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 8
      nanos: 945328403
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
