  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Color Scheme**\n\nI\'m working on the color palette. I\'ve pinpointed that the app needs to use black, purple, and white, with a dark default and a light mode option. Currently, I\'m analyzing the existing color scheme, which uses `slate-950` and `emerald-500`, to determine how best to incorporate the new colors.\n\n\n**Refining Color Palette**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the specific Tailwind classes. I\'ve decided on `bg-zinc-950` or `#090714` for dark mode and `bg-zinc-50` for light mode. I am aiming for vibrant purple accents with `purple-600`, etc., while ensuring the light mode utilizes `bg-purple-600` and `text-purple-600`. The theme toggle will be added in ProfileView or Header, and I have planned dark/light support via `dark` class toggling.\n\n\n**Expanding Document Support**\n\nI\'m now integrating document uploads for songs. My focus is enabling users to upload up to five documents per song, supporting PDFs, images, and other file types, like handwritten chords. I\'ve defined a `SongDocument` interface for this purpose, with fields for ID, name, type, data URL, file size, and creation date. The `CatalogSong` type will be updated to include an optional `documents` array. I plan to incorporate display options in `CatalogView`, `FocusedBlockView`, `SetlistDetail`, and the `CifraWebviewModal`.\n\n\n**Implementing File Uploads**\n\nI\'m now integrating file uploads for songs. My focus is enabling users to upload up to five documents per song, including PDFs and images. For the \"Cifra Club\" button, I\'m changing the icon to `<Guitar className=\"w-4 h-4\" />` with tooltip \"Cifra Club\", and using `<FileMusic className=\"w-4 h-4\" />` or `<Paperclip className=\"w-4 h-4\" />` for \"Partituras / Arquivos\". I plan to show a modal/drawer for upload, preview, and deletion, and to connect the database to Supabase.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 395015752
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
