    thinking: "**Triggering Background Sync**\n\nI\'ve been exploring ways to automate data synchronization with Supabase. I\'m focusing on triggering a background sync in `notifySubscribers()` when the `.env` config specifies it. I\'m also considering doing this automatically when the `App` component mounts, or when the `StorageEngine` initializes. I want to ensure the latest data is available with minimal effort.\n\n\n**Implementing Auto Sync**\n\nI\'ve decided to refine the automatic sync implementation. Currently, `notifySubscribers()` triggers `triggerAutoSync()` which debounces for 1 second before calling `syncLocalDataToSupabase()`, which checks for Supabase config. I\'m also adding this trigger in `App.tsx` on mount, checking for the presence of the required Supabase config keys. I\'m starting by attempting to implement the sync via the trigger in `notifySubscribers`.\n\n\n**Refining Remote Data Fetch**\n\nI\'ve incorporated a `try...catch` block around the Supabase data fetching and saving in `autoCloudInit()` to handle potential errors during the initial sync. I\'m checking for the presence of the `url` and `anonKey` config, and if present, I\'m fetching data. If successful, local storage is updated, otherwise, if the remote data is empty, I\'m attempting to sync local seed data to the cloud. I\'m also addressing the user\'s feedback in `ProfileView.tsx`, removing the Supabase synchronization card, focusing on automation.\n\n\n"
