  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing File Upload**\n\nI\'m currently focused on incorporating file upload functionality into the \"Nova M\303\272sica\" creation modal within `CatalogView.tsx`. I\'m starting by importing the necessary components from `lucide-react` and defining the expected `SongDocument` type. My immediate goal is to design the file upload section within the modal\'s structure. I\'m exploring how to best handle the state and visual representation for file attachments.\n\n\n**Implementing File Upload Logic**\n\nI\'ve implemented the core logic for handling file uploads. I\'m using state to manage the `newDocuments` array. The `handleNewDocFileUpload` function is responsible for processing file selections, including validation for file size (10MB limit) and quantity (maximum 5). I\'m also including file type detection, and utilizing `FileReader` to create data URLs for each uploaded file, which are then stored in the `SongDocument` array.\n\n\n**Refining File Handling**\n\nI\'ve been working on refining the file handling process within the song creation modal. I\'m focusing on how the uploaded documents interact with the song data when saved. When the song is saved, I\'m integrating the uploaded documents into the `StorageEngine.addCatalogSong` function. Also, after successful song creation, I reset the state variables related to the form, including the `newDocuments` array, and clear the input\'s selection. I\'m also ensuring the UI clearly displays the number of uploaded documents, with a maximum limit of five. I am also planning on rendering a button to remove existing uploaded files.\n\n\n**Visualizing File Previews**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a preview list for the uploaded files. I\'m dynamically rendering each `SongDocument` with its name, size, and an appropriate icon (PDF, image, or music). I\'m displaying the file size in KB and am also including logic to handle different file types, adapting the rendered icon. I plan to add a button to remove existing uploaded files. I\'m also ensuring the UI elements are appropriately styled using Tailwind classes.\n\n\n**Adding Remove File Functionality**\n\nI\'ve incorporated a button within the file preview list to remove individual uploaded documents. The logic uses `handleRemoveNewDoc`, triggered by the button\'s `onClick`, to update the state of the document array and remove the file. The UI is updated dynamically with the file removal.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 10
      nanos: 246258133
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
